      <activity id="20556d54-452b-514e-8374-f62a1faa9deb" activityNameId="5f11904f-20c1-52d3-98ca-7c5d9bd837ea" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Yarn production, cotton fibres</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Yarn production, cotton fibres
Inventory refers to the processing of 1 kg lint cotton only, without the production of the cotton itself.;
UUID: 37b6099c-6662-3634-8c61-878b0d3c3b8d
The inventories include energy consumption, transport and infrastructure related to the processing of lint cotton to yarn (cleaning, cardening, spinning).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Cardening and spinning are the main processes of the yarn production. Mechanical cleaning and no chemical cleaning was assumed for this study. 
Time period: undefined
Production volume:  
Sampling: Data were compiled from literature.  
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_37b6099c-6662-3634-8c61-878b0d3c3b8d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
